["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/ManufactureAction", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "ManufactureAction represents the act of creating a product by a manufacturing process.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/responsibilityChangedOn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The element that has its responsibility changed.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/orcidid", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[Open Researcher and Contributor ID (ORCID) iD](https://info.orcid.org/what-is-orcid/) is a unique identifier for authors and contributors in scholarly communication; as a subset of the International Standard Name Identifier (ISNI), it typically appears as a URI such as `https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ContactType/securityVulnerability", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A contact for reporting security vulnerabilities.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
